; ONE VARIABLE: `layout_direction = 3` (RTL) on the lower TabBar.
;
; Both bars are too narrow for their four tabs with `clip_tabs = true`, so
; `buttons_visible` turns on and the scroll arrows draw. Under RTL the pair
; moves from the trailing edge to the LEADING one, the second arrow steps by
; the INCREMENT icon's own width rather than the decrement's, and
; `missing_right` lights the DECREMENT arrow instead of the increment one
; (tab_bar.cpp:565-591) — three swaps that a bar without overflow never
; reaches, which is why `unit-tab-bar-rtl` (no clipping, icon and close
; buttons instead) cannot see a regression in any of them. Both bars anchor
; to the same symmetric rect, so only the inside of the strip can move.

